DSP components and algorithm reference

The dynamics compressor, convolution normalization and equal-power spatial
algorithms reference Chromium 148.0.7778.280 Blink audio sources. Original
Google/Apple copyright notices and redistribution conditions are preserved
verbatim in licenses/third-party/chromium-audio-148.0.7778.280, including the
source and binary redistribution conditions of each referenced component.
The native Rust implementations retain those notices and use fixed storage,
explicit resource ownership, media timing and device handover.

Original convolution impulse responses

The 13 lossless WAV files in assets/impulses are the original resources exported
by LX Music Desktop v2.12.6, commit ad95d5091c9ed689fa72b5e5c849df65f5a679ce,
from src/renderer/assets/medias/filters. Preset identifiers and linear gains
follow that commit's src/renderer/plugins/player/index.ts. The asset manifest
preserves the individual upstream URLs, SHA-256 digests and PCM geometry.
Upstream copyright and attribution remain with lyswhut and LX Music contributors
and the applicable original resource authors. The complete upstream root license
and supplementary terms are preserved in licenses/upstream; including these
assets does not grant commercial permission beyond those applicable terms.

The native FFT path uses RustFFT 6.4.1 and its locked numerical dependencies:
primal-check 0.3.4, strength_reduce 0.2.4, transpose 0.2.3, num-complex 0.4.6,
num-integer 0.1.47, num-traits 0.2.19, and the autocfg 1.5.1 build tool.
Their original MIT and Apache-2.0 texts are preserved in licenses/third-party.

The native pitch processor is implemented in Rust with reference to the Phaze
peak-region design (https://github.com/olvb/phaze) and the fixed LX Music Desktop
worklet reference above. The Phaze Unlicense is preserved in
licenses/third-party/phaze/LICENSE. FFT operations use RustFFT; the reference
JavaScript FFT source is not included in this implementation.
Component versions, upstream references and local license paths are listed in
docs/dsp-licenses.md.

